WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.838 --> 00:00:04.207
let it rest and get back to 100%

00:00:04.207 --> 00:00:04.474
next year.

00:00:04.607 --> 00:00:05.809
I was able to do what I needed

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:07.143
to do on the football field.

00:00:07.277 --> 00:00:09.179
&gt;&gt; It was incredible.

00:00:09.312 --> 00:00:12.415
Super bowl LVII was memorable

00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:14.317
and historic for a lot of

00:00:14.451 --> 00:00:14.718
reasons.

00:00:14.851 --> 00:00:17.620
One of them is this is the first

00:00:17.754 --> 00:00:19.122
time in the NFL that both

00:00:19.255 --> 00:00:20.357
starting quarterbacks were

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.458
black.

00:00:21.591 --> 00:00:22.659
There's a lot of that just

00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:24.494
rooted in some really bad

00:00:24.627 --> 00:00:25.729
unfairness in NFL history.

00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:27.597
But beyond that, what did it

00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:28.965
mean to you?

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:30.533
Did you and Jalen hurts, the

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.235
quarterback for the eagles, did

00:00:32.235 --> 00:00:35.438
you talk about it at all?

00:00:35.572 --> 00:00:37.040
&gt;&gt; It was talked about for sure.

00:00:37.173 --> 00:00:38.441
It was a special moment.

00:00:38.575 --> 00:00:39.743
I was glad that the game went

00:00:39.876 --> 00:00:41.277
the way it went, even though it

00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:44.447
made me a little nervous at the

00:00:44.581 --> 00:00:44.714
end.

00:00:44.848 --> 00:00:46.683
But Jalen played his tail off,

00:00:46.816 --> 00:00:46.950
man.

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:48.485
All respect to him.

00:00:48.618 --> 00:00:50.820
It showed that the black

00:00:50.954 --> 00:00:52.255
quarterback -- we've always been

00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:54.524
able to do, can go out and have

00:00:54.657 --> 00:00:55.658
success on the world stage in

00:00:55.792 --> 00:00:57.727
the biggest game of them all.

00:00:57.861 --> 00:00:59.329
We're standing on the shoulders

00:00:59.462 --> 00:01:01.664
of Doug Harris, Warren moon,

00:01:01.798 --> 00:01:03.166
Shaq Harris, all the greats.

00:01:03.299 --> 00:01:05.035
They gave us this platform and

00:01:05.168 --> 00:01:06.369
hopefully we can inspire some

00:01:06.503 --> 00:01:07.804
kids to follow their dream and

00:01:07.937 --> 00:01:09.506
be a quarterback in the future

00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:11.441
whenever we're sitting on the

00:01:11.574 --> 00:01:12.609
couch watching a super bowl.

00:01:12.742 --> 00:01:14.277
&gt;&gt; You talk about faith a lot.

00:01:14.411 --> 00:01:15.678
I'm wondering what's the best

00:01:15.812 --> 00:01:17.547
way you think your faith plays a

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.215
role in your game?

00:01:19.349 --> 00:01:22.652
Is it bringing you a peace?

00:01:22.786 --> 00:01:24.954
Does it bring you a perspective?

00:01:25.088 --> 00:01:29.025
How does it help you?

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:30.794
&gt;&gt; It's definitely perspective I

00:01:30.927 --> 00:01:32.562
think to me.

00:01:32.762 --> 00:01:34.330
I do a lot of just thinking

00:01:34.464 --> 00:01:35.932
about going out there and

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:37.834
playing to glorify him.

00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:39.702
It's not about winning and

00:01:39.836 --> 00:01:40.904
losing even though it is in our

00:01:41.037 --> 00:01:41.204
world.

00:01:41.337 --> 00:01:42.639
But it's to go out there and

00:01:42.772 --> 00:01:43.940
leave everything I have on the

00:01:44.307 --> 00:01:46.576
field to show that I'm

00:01:46.709 --> 00:01:47.210
glorifying him.

00:01:47.343 --> 00:01:49.112
It gives me perspective to leave

